{"name":"Cannon Barrel","hex":"#3c4142","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cannon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete assembly, consisting of an artillery tube and a breech mechanism, firing mechanism or base cap, which is a component of a gun, howitzer or mortar, which may include muzzle appendages.","Any similar device for shooting material out of a tube."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bombard with cannons.","To play the carom billiard shot; to strike two balls with the cue ball."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cannon"},{"term":"barrel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round (cylindrical) vessel, such as a cask, of greater length than breadth, and bulging in the middle, made of staves bound with hoops, and having flat ends (heads). The word is sometimes applied to a similar cylindrical container made of metal, usually called a drum.","Such a cask of a certain size, holding one-eighth of what a tun holds. (See a diagram comparing cask sizes.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put or to pack in a barrel or barrels.","To move quickly or in an uncontrolled manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cannon","blocks":[{"text":"A cannon is a large-caliber gun classified as a type of artillery, which usually launches a projectile using explosive chemical propellant. Gunpowder was the primary propellant before the invention of smokeless powder during the late 19th century. Cannons vary in gauge, effective range, mobility, rate of fire, angle of fire and firepower; different forms of cannon combine and balance these attributes in varying degrees, depending on their intended use on the battlefield. A cannon is a type of heavy artillery weapon. The word cannon is derived from several languages, in which the original definition can usually be translated as tube, cane, or reed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg/330px-%28Saint-Lys%29_Fauconneau_de_1589.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannon","wikidata":"Q81103"},{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel","wikidata":"Q10289"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg/500px-Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg/1280px-Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg/500px-Yuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bronze cannon with inscription dated the 3rd year of the Zhiyuan era (1332) of the Yuan dynasty (1271–1368); it was discovered at the Yunju Temple of Fangshan District, Beijing in 1935.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYuan_Bronze_Cannon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Ming_Dynasty_field_artillery_cannon.jpg/500px-Ming_Dynasty_field_artillery_cannon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/